# api-gateway Worker secrets for local development.
# `pnpm dev` always selects env.development from wrangler.jsonc and requires its
# remote `TRADING_RPC` VPC Service binding. There is no direct-URL fallback.
#
# In production, set secrets with:  wrangler secret put <NAME>
# Non-secret config goes in wrangler.jsonc under `vars`.
# `TRADING_RPC` is a binding, never a plaintext variable. Wrangler must be
# authenticated because the development binding uses `remote: true`.
#
# Use the same development signing secret as services/admin-rpc/.env.sample so
# the full local login flow works. Outside development provision a unique secret
# with:
#   wrangler secret put JWT_SECRET --env production
JWT_SECRET=local-jwt-secret-at-least-32-characters
#
